    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0099" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quebec</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-14">September 14, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Friend</hi>, I understand that we are meeting
                    at 11:30<anchor n="1" xml:id="d69-f1"/> about Stage
                        2. Dick Law arrived here late last night, and I wonder whether I
                    might bring him at 11 o’clock with or without Anthony,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d69-f2"/> to discuss the application of U.N.R.R.A. to Italy. He tells me that a compromise proposal would
                    get through whereby 50 million dollars of U.N.R.R.A. would be available for Italy. I consider this should be
                    an essential part of our friendly gesture to Italy.</p>
                <p>If agreeable then, I will turn up at 11.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d69-f3"/></p>
                <p>Yours always,</p>
                <closer><signed>W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">inston S.
                    Churchill</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d69-f1" n="1" xml:id="d69-f1-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg342">p. 342</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d69-f2" n="2" xml:id="d69-f2-content">
                <p>Eden.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d69-f3" n="3" xml:id="d69-f3-content">
                <p>No record of the discussion at the 11 o’clock meeting between Roosevelt and
                    Churchill on September 14 has been found.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
